#====================================================================
# Draft knowledge entry - local hardcoded env fallbacks must never override
#   the variables a tool_requires (automake/libtool) already provides
# Source package: qatlib/26.02.0 (PERL5LIB clobbered automake/1.18's value)
#====================================================================

id:                     DRAFT-ohos-tool-requires-buildenv-must-not-be-overridden-by-local-fallbacks
trigger_tool:           conan|autoconf|automake|aclocal|autoreconf|perl
phase:                  configuration|build

error_signature:        Can't locate Automake/Config\.pm in @INC|Can't locate .*\.pm in @INC.*automake|automake-1\.16: not found|autoreconf: error: .*aclocal failed|BEGIN failed--compilation aborted at .*aclocal

severity:               2
category:               autotools, conan, packaging, environment, build-system
match_keywords:         OHOS, conan, tool_requires, buildenv_info, VirtualBuildEnv, PERL5LIB, ACLOCAL_PATH, AUTOMAKE, ACLOCAL, automake, libtool, aclocal, autoreconf, hardcoded fallback, clobber, override, @INC, qatlib

title:                  When a recipe declares tool_requires(automake), its buildenv_info is authoritative - local hardcoded fallbacks must be applied only for variables it did not set

root_cause:             A recipe that bootstraps autotools (sdist has no configure, so
                        autoreconf must run) declares tool_requires("automake/1.18") and
                        tool_requires("libtool/2.5.4"), then expands VirtualBuildEnv into
                        the subprocess environment because it uses subprocess.run(env=...)
                        instead of self.run(env="conanbuild").  The trap is a second layer
                        of "safety" fallbacks left over from before the tool_requires were
                        added: unconditional assignments such as
                        env["PERL5LIB"] = ".../usr/local/share/automake-1.16" and
                        env["AUTOMAKE"] / env["ACLOCAL"] = /storage/.../usr/local/bin/...
                        That directory belongs to the CI image, is version-skewed (1.16 vs
                        the tool_require's 1.18) and - decisively - it REPLACES the value
                        the automake package itself supplied.  automake/1.18 ships
                        relocatable wrapper scripts whose @INC is installed with a broken
                        prefix (the log shows a literal `//share/automake-1.18`), and it is
                        precisely its own PERL5LIB (pointing at its real
                        share/automake-1.18) that makes those scripts load their modules.
                        Overwriting it breaks aclocal, which then cannot find its own
                        modules: "Can't locate Automake/Config.pm in @INC".

affected_scope:         Any recipe that (a) obtains autotools from tool_requires rather
                        than from the host image, and (b) still carries hardcoded absolute
                        paths for the same variables (PERL5LIB, AUTOMAKE, ACLOCAL,
                        ACLOCAL_PATH, AUTOCONF, ...).  Measured on qatlib 26.02.0
                        (CI #65764): declaring the tool_requires fixed the earlier
                        "Can't exec aclocal" failure, and the leftover PERL5LIB assignment
                        immediately produced a new failure inside aclocal itself.

verification_cmd:       grep -nE 'env\["(PERL5LIB|AUTOMAKE|ACLOCAL|ACLOCAL_PATH)"\] *=' archives/<pkg>/*/conanfile.py

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           tool-requires-values-authoritative-fallbacks-guarded
rec_description:        Expand the tool_requires' environment first and record which keys
                        it actually provided, then apply every local fallback ONLY for keys
                        that are absent - never assign over a provided value:
                          vbe = VirtualBuildEnv(self).vars()
                          env.update(vbe.items())
                          provided = set(vbe.keys())
                          if "PERL5LIB" not in provided:        # guarded
                              ... set the local fallback ...
                          for k, v in (...local per-tool paths...):
                              if k in provided:                 # guarded
                                  continue
                              ... set only if the file exists ...
                        autoconf/m4 may legitimately stay SDK-provided (declaring
                        autoconf/2.72 pulls an OHOS perl whose XS conflicts with the SDK
                        perl used by autoreconf), so the guard - not the fallback's
                        deletion - is what keeps both paths working.
rec_command:            python -c "from conan.tools.env import VirtualBuildEnv; vbe=VirtualBuildEnv(conanfile).vars(); env.update(vbe.items()); provided=set(vbe.keys())"
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               recipe-source-layout

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      drop-the-fallbacks-entirely-once-tool-requires-are-declared
fallback_description:   If the tool_requires is reliably resolvable in every build
                        environment (it is in the registry and L0i verifies it), the
                        hardcoded fallbacks can be removed outright rather than guarded.
                        Keeping them guarded is the safer default because the fallbacks
                        also cover the SDK-provided autoconf/m4, which are deliberately
                        NOT declared as tool_requires.
fallback_command:       conan search automake/* -r=ohpcd
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          dependency-resolution

forbid_1_pattern:       env\["PERL5LIB"\] *= *["'].*usr/local/share/automake|env\["(AUTOMAKE|ACLOCAL)"\] *= *["']/storage
forbid_1_reason:        An unguarded assignment silently replaces the value the automake
                        tool_require contributed; its relocated scripts then cannot load
                        their own modules, and the error surfaces inside aclocal - far from
                        the line that caused it.
forbid_1_consequence:   A new failure immediately after the tool_requires were added,
                        easily misread as 'the tool_requires did not work / automake is
                        broken', leading to reverting a correct fix.

forbid_2_pattern:       hardcode .*/storage/Users/currentUser/usr/local/.*automake|rely on the CI image's automake version
forbid_2_reason:        The image's automake is version-skewed relative to the declared
                        tool_require (1.16 vs 1.18) and is not part of the recipe's
                        dependency graph, so the build is not reproducible across workers.
forbid_2_consequence:   Builds that pass on one worker and fail on another, or after the
                        image is updated, with no recipe change to explain it.

forbid_3_pattern:       remove tool_requires\(automake|revert.*tool_requires.*because.*aclocal|blame automake/1\.18
forbid_3_reason:        The tool_requires is the correct fix; the failure was caused by the
                        local override defeating it.  Reverting reintroduces the original
                        'Can't exec aclocal' problem.
forbid_3_consequence:   Oscillation between two failures without converging, each round
                        attributed to the wrong cause.

similar_to:             [DRAFT-perl-buildenv-info-missing-dependency-injection, DRAFT-cpdb-libs-1.2.0-autotools-git-archive-tool-requires-bootstrap, DRAFT-remctl-3.18-conan-buildenv-save-order]
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []

notes_diff_vs_perl_buildenv:  DRAFT-perl-buildenv-info-missing-dependency-injection is the
                        OPPOSITE direction: there the dependency declares only runenv_info,
                        so PERL5LIB never reaches the build context and the consumer must
                        inject it itself.  Here the variable IS provided (buildenv_info)
                        and the consumer must be careful not to overwrite it.  Together
                        they bracket the same variable: missing -> inject; provided ->
                        do not clobber.
notes_diff_vs_cpdb:     DRAFT-cpdb-libs-1.2.0-autotools-git-archive-tool-requires-bootstrap
                        establishes that git-archive/no-dist tarballs need
                        tool_requires automake+libtool.  This entry starts after that is
                        done: what happens to the leftover host-image fallbacks once the
                        tool_requires are in place.
notes_diff_vs_remctl:   DRAFT-remctl-3.18-conan-buildenv-save-order is about the ORDER in
                        which conan saves buildenv files; this entry is about a hand-written
                        assignment defeating a tool_require's contribution.
notes_diagnosis_order:  Read the @INC entries in the error literally - they list which
                        directories were searched and in which order.  Seeing the
                        tool_require's own share dir AND a foreign usr/local/share/automake-1.16
                        side by side is the tell that a local assignment is competing with
                        the tool_require.
notes_qatlib:           qatlib 26.02.0: after tool_requires("automake/1.18") fixed
                        'Can't exec "aclocal"', the leftover
                        env["PERL5LIB"] = "/storage/Users/currentUser/usr/local/share/automake-1.16"
                        caused "Can't locate Automake/Config.pm in @INC (@INC entries
                        checked: //share/automake-1.18 /storage/.../usr/local/share/
                        automake-1.16 ...) at .../bin/.aclocal-real line 33".
                        Guarding each fallback with `if k not in provided` fixed it.
